{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1168846-moonsilver-s-potential-for-cyclical-change","id":1168846,"title":"Moonsilver's potential for cyclical change","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-19T10:38:49-08:00","id":1168846,"title":"Moonsilver's potential for cyclical change","content":"The difficulty of cyclical changes for weapons is that they are predictable. A weapon that changes forms according to a consistent schedule is more easily countered by an enemy who chooses the time and place of confrontation.<br /> <br /> There are ways to mitigate this vulnerability, and even turn the predictability into a strength.<br /> <br /> For example, a magical barrier cast over a kingdom could might render it cut off from four of five directions of approach, with the opening changing with the cycle of the moon or seasons. While enemies can easily plot to exploit the timing of the opening they most desire, the kingdom's defenders are always able to concentrate their forces at the one place they too can predict to be their most (if not only) vulnerable location.<br /> <br /> Even if the barrier only barred entrance from one of five directions, the defenders could spare themselves the effort of guarding that one direction in favor of minding the other four.<br /> <br /> Offensively, the use of cyclical changes seems best exploited with assassins' weapons, or other tools meant to be used without warning against someone denied the ability to choose the time or place of confrontation.<br /> <br /> For example, an assassin's chakram which taps into the cycle of the moon's phases for killing power. If used to wound a victim the first night of the new moon, the chakram builds energy over time; an attack half-way through through the moon's cycle will be more deadly; an attack on the next night of the exact same phase will be deadlier still.<br /> <br /> Even if the victim knows the weapon's power, predicting the timing of the assassin's next attack becomes a mind game. Will the assassin wait for the half-way time, the entire month, or simply attack again the very same night as soon as the victim lets his guard down?<br /> <br /> And that ignores the potential for a master of the weapon to incite it into a rapid cycle of changes, where it counts each round of combat as a lunar phase, counting down eight turns to the victim's unstoppable death.<br /> <br /> Thoughts, opinions, any other ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T10:52:59-08:00","id":1168850,"title":"","content":"I have no strong feelings about actual moon-phase timing, but I'm envisioning a weapon that cycles through benefits each action regardless of whether it's used that way or not. If you get the timing right it's very good, but missing a step in the cycle could ruin your advantage. I feel like the benefits would have to be pretty strong to offset the drawbacks. Like Action 1 is bonus initiative gain on a withering attack , Action 2 is bonus on a Decisive attack, and action 3 is bonus on Disengage. Maybe each bonus comes with a drawback if you do a different kind of action, like a rock-paper-scissors style thing. It'd be situationally very useful and situationally bad, but I find those weapons to be the most interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T11:03:51-08:00","id":1168857,"title":"","content":"For starters, I think that barrier you just described would be a phenomenal Celestial/Solar sorcerous working. Secondly, I love how the changing barrier just begs questions about logistics, commerce, and strategy.<br /> <br /> For instance, how quickly do the entrances change. If it is instantaneous, it becomes critically important to move troops to the new entrance ahead of time. Depending on the size of the kingdom, the time that it takes to move those troops could mean that there are weeks to months where the gates are staffed by a lessened force. This could mean that a daring strategist could perform a pincer attack by charging one of the openings just as they close while keeping a force outside of the one about to open. A suicide mission, surely. But if you're an Exalt with sorcerer-circlemate who can spare a pack of demons, it could be a valid strategy.<br /> <br /> If four of five directions are closed, it can make blockading and sieging a whole kingdom trivially easy to a sufficiently sized army. Depending on the size and trade needs of the kingdom, this could turn their impenetrable defense into nation-sized coffin.<br /> <br /> For commerce and diplomacy, depending on the size of the kingdom, there could be whole portions of the year where it is effectively closed for communications and trade with neighbors in 4 of 5 directions. This could create scenarios where diplomats have to operate in the dark and unable to send messages and where the barrier may open to reveal that there have been regime changes that turned once reliable allies into new enemies. Similarly, it could mean that certain commodities wax and wane in price reliably as direct routes towards their origin open and close. All of this would be super exploitable for a group of enterprising PCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1168846-moonsilver-s-potential-for-cyclical-change?p=1168850#post1168850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no strong feelings about actual moon-phase timing, but I'm envisioning a weapon that cycles through benefits each action regardless of whether it's used that way or not. If you get the timing right it's very good, but missing a step in the cycle could ruin your advantage. I feel like the benefits would have to be pretty strong to offset the drawbacks. Like Action 1 is bonus initiative gain on a withering attack , Action 2 is bonus on a Decisive attack, and action 3 is bonus on Disengage. Maybe each bonus comes with a drawback if you do a different kind of action, like a rock-paper-scissors style thing. It'd be situationally very useful and situationally bad, but I find those weapons to be the most interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or how about a suit of armor that hardens against weapons with the same tags as the last thing to attack it. I would imagine it could turn somebody night invulnerable against a battlegroup with uniform weaponry but leave them vulnerable to, say, a squad of unique fighters with different weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":5526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","user":"Steamfunk","date":". 12-19-2017, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T11:15:10-08:00","id":1168860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1168846-moonsilver-s-potential-for-cyclical-change?p=1168857#post1168857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or how about a suit of armor that hardens against weapons with the same tags as the last thing to attack it. I would imagine it could turn somebody night invulnerable against a battlegroup with uniform weaponry but leave them vulnerable to, say, a squad of unique fighters with different weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo I like this idea. A variety of evocations just popped into my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T11:44:37-08:00","id":1168866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1168846-moonsilver-s-potential-for-cyclical-change?p=1168860#post1168860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooo I like this idea. A variety of evocations just popped into my head.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Go for it, I would love to see what you do with it. The general idea I had for it is that it is an armor of &quot;learning and forgetting.&quot; It provides all sorts of powers for beating enemies that try to use the same charms, weapons, actions, and influences multiple times but fails against diversified assaults. I also thought resonant characters might get options to track multiple sources of actions rather than treating all actions against the wielder as coming from the same source - IE: one for the main opponent and one for everybody else in a scene so that the wearer can isolate more dangerous opponents for responses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T12:09:13-08:00","id":1168876,"title":"","content":"Adaptation is suitably moonsilver, but it is not cyclic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T07:53:09-08:00","id":1169089,"title":"","content":"Speaking to the cyclical nature of moonsilver, it doesn't have to be the lunar cycle it's linked to. <br /> <br /> You could do something like a pendulum or a metronome for the back forth of combat eventually gaining momentum and destructive power.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps you could emulate the tides or other cyclical phenomenon without actually being linked to the turning of the tides in any way. <br /> <br /> You could even do something where you have a repeating set of effects that you touch off with some type of action or other such that you're in control of the artifact's cycles without changing the fact that it goes through cycles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T08:27:51-08:00","id":1169094,"title":"","content":"A weapon can be cyclic without necessarily having those cycles all happen within a single battle, too. A weapon could have a cycle tied to the seasons, for instance, with spring giving healing to the wielder and their allies, summer giving extra damage and ferocity to the wielder's attacks, autumn being particularly strong against undead (&quot;laying the dead to rest&quot;), and winter having abilities to slow and hinder enemies. If the &quot;season&quot; the weapon is in can only change once per combat, you have a setup where the wielder will want to try to match the battle to the season the weapon is in, on a strategic level rather than a tactical, and the opportunity to change seasons to deal with a changed situation is a real struggle, because it will mean at least 3 more battles will have to happen before you can switch back to the current season.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T08:44:16-08:00","id":1169098,"title":"","content":"That said, the lunar cycle is really evocative. <br /> <br /> My original idea for the assassin's chakram, and the one that I still want to use, is that it changes itself to more effectively harm certain origins of creature depending on the current lunar phase.<br /> <br /> During the new moon and Calibration, the chakram counters demons. During the full moon, the weapon counters anything of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> The other three phases could be devoted to Elementals, the restless dead, and Gods, with a Resonant effect allowing the Elemental and God phases to apply against Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals.<br /> <br /> But there are twice as many crescent, half, and gibbous phases as new and full phases.<br /> <br /> It would make sense for a post-Usurpation weapon to be most effective against Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals twice as often as actual enemies of humanity.<br /> <br /> If the weapon was made after the reveal of the Abyssal Exalted, it would also make sense for the waxing phases to harm the Exalted who correspond to the spirits harmed by the waning phases, for a total of eight different forms.<br /> <br /> None of which include Lunars or Solars, which seems just fine if these baneful forms (or at least the anti-Exalt applications) are locked behind the Resonant keyword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T17:26:34-08:00","id":1169232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1168846-moonsilver-s-potential-for-cyclical-change?p=1169089#post1169089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking to the cyclical nature of moonsilver, it doesn't have to be the lunar cycle it's linked to. <br /> <br /> You could do something like a pendulum or a metronome for the back forth of combat eventually gaining momentum and destructive power.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps you could emulate the tides or other cyclical phenomenon without actually being linked to the turning of the tides in any way. <br /> <br /> You could even do something where you have a repeating set of effects that you touch off with some type of action or other such that you're in control of the artifact's cycles without changing the fact that it goes through cycles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been playing with the idea of an artifact that can be changed into different weapons, each with a unique power/Evocation or with each Evocation operating differently depending on the current form. Tying it to a thematic cycle could be a cool way to work that, but I think it would operate best if successfully using the power of one weapon triggered the next phase of the cycle, rather than having it swap forms every round automatically.<br /> <br /> If designed correctly, you might not even need to have it automatically swap, since activating, say, Summer Growth would set the target up so that Autumnal Reaping gets a big boost, so the person using it would be likely to follow the cycle directly. But it depends on how much you want the cycle to define the weapon, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Just make sure that the various points of the cycle can be useful when they're active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T06:46:42-08:00","id":1169331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1168846-moonsilver-s-potential-for-cyclical-change?p=1169089#post1169089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking to the cyclical nature of moonsilver, it doesn't have to be the lunar cycle it's linked to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did suggest the seasonal cycle for the kingdom barrier. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could do something like a pendulum or a metronome for the back forth of combat eventually gaining momentum and destructive power. </div> </div> </div>Like Moonlit Huntress, but functional and with interesting Evocations. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or perhaps you could emulate the tides or other cyclical phenomenon without actually being linked to the turning of the tides in any way. </div> </div> </div>The only idea that comes to mind right now is Moonlit Huntress, but made of black jade. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could even do something where you have a repeating set of effects that you touch off with some type of action or other such that you're in control of the artifact's cycles without changing the fact that it goes through cycles. </div> </div> </div>Oh, I hadn\u2019t considered that. Wish it sparked a specific idea in me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T06:48:11-08:00","id":1169332,"title":"","content":"That's the trick, isn't it.<br /> <br /> Cyclical weapons are kinda the opposite of adaptable weapons actually. Being trapped in a cycle forces you to act in a certain way. When applied properly, this can be devastating and awesome, but it does mean you can't adapt to fit the situation as easily. <br /> <br /> I just realized that cyclical weapons may also trap the <i>player</i> into repetitive actions if poorly implemented. Doing the same thing in sequence for every fight doesn't sound like a lot of fun for the player after a while. Something to keep in mind when designing these weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T06:55:53-08:00","id":1169337,"title":"","content":"One thing to keep in mind is that you don\u2019t need to punish someone for breaking a cycle, just reward them for completing each step of one.<br /> <br /> That helps someone be flexible when necessary, as they don\u2019t lose any ability to deal with unexpected situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T10:22:46-08:00","id":1169398,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how much I'd enjoy tracking all of that. <br /> <br /> What I might do is let such an Artifact phase according to the desire of the player, and let them nominate one Evocation to get a buff for the duration of a Scene. Make it less expensive to activate or extend duration from instant to tick, or turn to scene, or some such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T08:44:47-08:00","id":1169641,"title":"","content":"A moonsilver javelin that mimics the lifecycle of the Ichenuemon Hunter bug monster.<br /> <br /> A decisive attack (Melee or Thrown) causes the javelin to invade the victim\u2019s body, where it continues to inflict internal damage until it bursts free and flies back to its master\u2019s hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}